From 04cde3193b6559f6df0e156e5676dcdd2af6cd7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:26:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Parse national own numbers and late modem country codes
 correctly

Two bugs made an incoming MMS on a Korean SIM list the user's own number
as a recipient and lose its attachments:

- ModemController::ownNumber() prepended '+' to every number, because
  QStringList::startsWith() compares the first element with "+" instead of
  testing its first character. ModemManager reports what the SIM stores,
  and a Korean SIM stores 010XXXXXXXX, so the own number became
  +010XXXXXXXX: unparseable, never equal to the parsed sender list, and
  never removed from it. Keep numbers that start with '+' or with a trunk
  prefix '0' as they are; no E.164 country code starts with 0.

- The daemon starts at login before the modem exists, so its constructor
  sets the PhoneNumber country code from the locale fallback. When the
  modem appears, checkMessages() refreshes the own number but not the
  country code, so national numbers stay unparsed until the daemon is
  restarted. The raw recipient list then hashes to a different
  attachments folder than the one the app looks in, and pictures show as
  "Cannot open". Refresh the country code in checkMessages() as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L5scTPdTNcEmdyRhJMbUHU
---
 daemon/channellogger.cpp                 |  5 +++++
 lib/telephonySupport/modemcontroller.cpp | 11 ++++++++---
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/daemon/channellogger.cpp b/daemon/channellogger.cpp
index e607a23..76a7a8a 100644
--- a/daemon/channellogger.cpp
+++ b/daemon/channellogger.cpp
@@ -72,6 +72,11 @@ ChannelLogger::ChannelLogger(std::optional<QString> &modemPath, QObject *parent)
 
 void ChannelLogger::checkMessages()
 {
+    // The daemon usually starts before ModemManager has a modem, so the
+    // country code set in the constructor came from the locale fallback.
+    // Take the modem's now, before any national number gets parsed.
+    PhoneNumber::setCountryCode(countryCode());
+
     // update own number
     m_ownNumber = PhoneNumber(ownNumber());
 
diff --git a/lib/telephonySupport/modemcontroller.cpp b/lib/telephonySupport/modemcontroller.cpp
index eba5f01..5716956 100644
--- a/lib/telephonySupport/modemcontroller.cpp
+++ b/lib/telephonySupport/modemcontroller.cpp
@@ -196,10 +196,15 @@ QString ModemController::ownNumber()
     const QStringList numbers = m_interface->ownNumbers();
 
     if (!numbers.isEmpty()) {
-        if (numbers.startsWith(QStringLiteral("+"))) {
-            return numbers.first();
+        const QString &number = numbers.first();
+        // ModemManager reports the MSISDN as the SIM stores it: E.164 with or
+        // without the '+', or a national number with its trunk prefix (Korean
+        // SIMs store 010...). No country code starts with 0, so only a number
+        // that starts with neither '+' nor '0' is an E.164 number missing its '+'.
+        if (number.startsWith(u'+') || number.startsWith(u'0')) {
+            return number;
         }
-        return QStringLiteral("+") + numbers.first();
+        return QStringLiteral("+") + number;
     }
 
     return QString();
